PURPOSE Convert feasible paths into the paper's separate route-column coefficients.
INPUT ArcResult, validated Plan or validated PricingCandidate; initialization tag
OUTPUT vehicle/package routes, ownership, coverage, service incidence and arc costs
REFERENCES A_B_generator.Generating_a_and_b; paper Eqs. 18-31

PROCEDURE ExtractSplitColumns(solution,initializationKind)
    IF solution is an ArcResult or Plan
        REQUIRE it contains a validated feasible Plan
        vehiclePaths := all physical vehicle paths in that plan
        packagePaths := all complete package paths in that plan
    ELSE IF solution is a PricingCandidate
        REQUIRE its actual owner path passes its local path/duty/branch checks
        vehiclePaths := its vehicle path if present, otherwise empty
        packagePaths := its complete package path if present, otherwise empty
        do not require an independently priced path to be a complete global Plan
    ELSE: return contract failure
    result := empty RoutePool
    FOR each (k,selected vehicle arcs) in vehiclePaths
        path := TracePath(selected vehicle arcs,source[k],sink[k])
        cost := sum(a in path) arcCost[k,a]
        g[l,kPrime] := 1 iff kPrime == k
        dVehicle[l,r] := service indicator of order r on path
            under the same paper definition used by master/pricing
        B[l,s] := incidence of supported state transition s on path
        emit VehicleRoute(l,k,path,cost,duration,g,dVehicle,B)
        retain a valid zero-cost unused vehicle route
    FOR each (r,selected package arcs) in packagePaths
        join r+/r- fragments at the same legal transfer location/time, if used
        path := TracePath(complete package arcs,source[r],sink[r])
        cost := sum(a in path) arcCost[r,a]
        dPackage[q,rPrime] := 1 iff rPrime == r
        b[q,s] := incidence of supported state transition s on path
        isUnserved := path uses the paper unserved choice
        emit PackageRoute(q,r,path,cost,dPackage,b,fragments,transfers,isUnserved)
        retain an unserved route as a penalized route choice, not physical service
    populate A/B dictionary views using the semantic mapping below
    CheckViews(result)
    return result

PROCEDURE Cost(arc,initializationKind)
    return arc.value under its declared paper/catalog convention
    initializationKind records provenance and does not overwrite physical costs

PROCEDURE TracePath(selected,source,sink)
    current := source; path := empty; remaining := set(selected)
    WHILE current != sink
        next := unused outgoing arc from current
        REQUIRE exactly one next arc and next not previously visited
        append next; remove next from remaining; current := next.head
    REQUIRE remaining is empty
    return path

PROCEDURE MergeColumn(pool,route)
    signature := catalogId,kind,ownerId,ordered original arc IDs,service incidence
    IF signature already present
        REQUIRE all costs and coefficients agree; return existing routeId
    assign fresh routeId; insert route, cost and every coefficient orientation
    retain paired-fragment references under one package route ID
    CheckViews(pool); return routeId

PROCEDURE RemoveRoutes(pool,routeIds)
    remove routes from costs, paths, g,dVehicle,dPackage,B,b and dictionary views
    remove their fragment associations; remove empty entries after traversal
    CheckViews(pool); return pool

NOTES
    g[l,k] records physical ownership; dVehicle[l,r] records service incidence.
    dPackage[q,r] covers a complete package choice, including an unserved route.
    A maps to service/coverage by route kind; B maps to that kind's arc incidence.
    Keep g,dVehicle,dPackage,B,b explicit when exposing A/A_transpose and
    B/B_transpose dictionaries.
    Independent pricing supplies locally feasible paths. A selected solution
    becomes an executable Plan after the global carrier/capacity audit.
